      "side": 1,
      "message": "The inclusion of `SkBlurDrawLooper.h` and `SkLayerDrawLooper.h` was an oversight masked by the fact that our Bazel build does *not* compile headers on its own (without us generating a .h.cpp file for the IWYU things). G3 *does* compile the headers and it noticed the missing header.\n\n`//include/core:legacy_draw_looper`, `//src/core:legacy_draw_looper`, and `//src/effects:legacy_draw_looper` are not used in other Bazel rules, but are used to generate .gni file lists for Chromium.\n\n\u003e At that point there is no reason to have the filegroups in subdirectories at all\n\nI disagree with this - I think it makes more sense to have filegroups in a folder that care about the files there (and possibly in subfolders) than having a huge, exhaustive file list somewhere (where? //src/core ? ick...).\n\nAs far as tracking which files need other files, that is the point of combining the filegroups into `cc_library`s, e.g. the modules (buffet entrees). I see no other tractable option given how many different folders our \"core\" functionality lives in. Our \"core\" build is a bit of a ball of mud, but not as big as it once was and I hope that future modules are similarly partitioned.",
      "parentUuid": "7020bb06_8ed77e13",
